rt math\n\ndef max_product_tuple(tuples_list):\n    max_product = -float('inf')\n    for t1 in tuples_list:\n        for t2 in tuples_list:\n            product = abs(t1[0] * t2[1])  # Pair (t1[0], t2[1])\n            if product > max_product:\n                max_product = product\n    return max_product\n```\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Test Cases:\n\n```python\nassert math.isclose(max_product_tuple([(2, 7), (2, 6), (1, 8), (4, 9)]), 36, rel_tol=0.001)\nassert math.isclose(max_product_tuple([(10,20), (15,2), (5,10)] ), 200, rel_tol=0.001)\nassert math.isclose(max_product_tuple([(11,44), (10,15), (20,5), (12, 9)] ), 484, rel_tol=0.001)\n```\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Explanation of Test Cases:\n\n1. `[(2, 7), (2, 6), (1, 8), (4, 9)]` \u2192 Max product is `4 * 9 = 36`\n2. `[(10,20), (15,2), (5,10)]` \u2192 Max product is `10 * 20 = 200`\n3. `[(11,44), (10,15), (20,5), (12, 9)]` \u2192 Max product is `11 * 44 = 484`\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n```python\nimport math\n\ndef max_product_tuple(tuples_list):\n    max_product = -float('inf')\n    for t1 in tuples_list:\n        for t2 in tuples_list:\n            product = abs(t1[0] * t2[1])\n            if product > max_product:\n                max_product = product\n    return max_product\n```", "decode_seconds": 8.549376093782485, "draft_calls": 149, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 214, "method": "native_target_eagle3", "output_hash": "8666865e370ad62a227b888a7e8d8e5e76d8d0545f498c82865da14ad0caa9d6", "output_tokens": 784, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23119230464, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23290970112, "problem_id": "Mbpp/120", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 3549.038282752037, "prefill_full_target": 36.89244842529297, "prefill_relay": 0.5146880149841309, "relay": 49.305472046136856, "unattributed_runtime": 139.15204656869173, "verification_full_target": 4774.473155975342}, "proposal_lengths": [7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7